[87.428141, "o", "\r\n\u001b[92mDone — the plot was saved, and here are the statistics for **Wind |B| at 3 s cadence over 2015-03-17 03:30–05:00 UTC**.\r\n\r\n**Parameter used:** `cda/WI_H0_MFI/B3GSE` (Wind MFI 3-second GSE Cartesian components). |B| was computed from the three GSE components with the NaN-safe magnitude helper — the magnitude is frame-independent, so GSE components are equivalent to any other frame.\r\n\r\n| Statistic | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Mean \\|B\\| | **19.788 nT** |\r\n| Minimum \\|B\\| | **8.682 nT** |\r\n| Maximum \\|B\\| | **28.286 nT** |\r\n\r\n- Valid points: 1770 of 1800 (expected 90 min at 3 s).\r\n- Note: there is one short data gap of 90 s (03:55:10.5 → 03:56:37.5 UTC), ~1.7% missing — below any concern threshold, and the statistics correctly excluded it via `nanmean`/`nanmin`/`nanmax`.\r\n\r\nThe time-series figure (with the mean shown as a dashed red reference line) has been saved to the workspace.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
